WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.883 --> 00:00:02.884
- [Elizabeth] Music is really,
really, really powerful

00:00:02.884 --> 00:00:07.504
in itself, and in what it can
do for you outside of music.

00:00:07.504 --> 00:00:10.754
(vibrant string music)

00:00:16.481 --> 00:00:17.816
- [Narrator] Korogocho
is one of the largest

00:00:17.816 --> 00:00:20.320
slum neighborhoods in Nairobi, Kenya,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.621
but do to extreme poverty,
there's limited access

00:00:22.621 --> 00:00:24.599
to youth arts programs.

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:27.069
Since 2008, a community
program called Ghetto Classics

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:28.709
has been trying to change that.

00:00:28.709 --> 00:00:30.346
(clarinet playing)

00:00:30.346 --> 00:00:32.311
- My name is Elizabeth Njoroge,

00:00:32.311 --> 00:00:34.287
and I'm the founder and director

00:00:34.287 --> 00:00:37.255
of the Ghetto Classics program.

00:00:37.255 --> 00:00:40.175
Ghetto Classics is a program

00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:42.245
that started off here in Karogocho.

00:00:42.245 --> 00:00:45.057
It's about using music to change the lives

00:00:45.057 --> 00:00:47.127
of young Kenyans,

00:00:47.127 --> 00:00:50.739
and, in particular, those from
very difficult environments

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:52.740
and backgrounds and lives.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.736
(recorder tooting)

00:00:54.736 --> 00:00:58.004
Korogocho is hard, but
we hope that in our space

00:00:58.004 --> 00:01:00.731
we are creating a better Korogocho.

00:01:00.731 --> 00:01:04.882
(lively orchestral music)

00:01:04.882 --> 00:01:06.610
We teach 600 kids a week.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.639
We have violins, one viola, the cellos.

00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:12.761
We have flute, clarinets, saxophones,

00:01:12.761 --> 00:01:15.263
tubas, trombones, trumpets.

00:01:15.263 --> 00:01:16.912
We only got French horns the other day,

00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:18.782
which is very exciting.

00:01:18.782 --> 00:01:21.260
We see that the discipline that
comes with the kind of music

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:24.909
that we teach, in this
case classical music,

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:26.750
um, is something very
important for these kids,

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.691
because it's something
they may lack at home.

00:01:28.691 --> 00:01:31.297
So they play together,
make music together,

00:01:31.297 --> 00:01:32.420
that gives them family.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.662
(saxophone plays)

00:01:34.662 --> 00:01:37.798
The lives of the kids are
just so, so, so difficult.

00:01:37.798 --> 00:01:39.839
The challenges they face.

00:01:39.839 --> 00:01:42.603
They've been crushed by life,

00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:45.936
having, you know, no hope when everybody around you

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.418
is just fighting to survive.

00:01:48.418 --> 00:01:51.187
So we hope that in our
space, we're creating a place

00:01:51.187 --> 00:01:55.354
where dreams can be nourished
and can grow and be fulfilled.

00:01:57.144 --> 00:01:59.727
(gentle music)

